+# SPEC: RadioList outline style
+
+## Objective
+Allow `RadioList<TValue>` and `RadioListGeneric<TValue>` in button mode (`IsButton="true"`) to render with Bootstrap outline buttons, so that unselected items show a colored border/text and the selected item is filled.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- New parameter `IsOutline` (bool, default `false`) on `RadioList<TValue>` and `RadioListGeneric<TValue>`.
+- With `IsButton && IsOutline`: every item gets `btn btn-outline-{Color}`; the selected item also gets `active` (no `bg-{Color}`); the group container gets `is-outline` (its own border is removed so the outline buttons don't double up).
+- With `IsOutline == false`, rendering is unchanged (`btn active bg-{Color}` for the selected item).
+- `IsOutline` has no effect when `IsButton` is false.
+- Demo + attribute docs + en-US/zh-CN localization updated.
+
+## Commands
+- Build: `dotnet build src/BootstrapBlazor`
+- Test: `dotnet test test/UnitTest --filter "FullyQualifiedName~Radio"`
+
+## Structure
+- `src/BootstrapBlazor/Components/Radio/RadioList.razor.cs`, `RadioListGeneric.razor.cs`, `RadioList.razor.scss`
+- `src/BootstrapBlazor.Server/Components/Samples/Radios.razor(.cs)`, `Locales/*.json`
+- Tests: `test/UnitTest/Components/RadioTest.cs`, `RadioListGenericTest.cs`
+
+## Code style
+Follow existing `CssBuilder` patterns and XML doc comments (Chinese summary, as in surrounding code).
+
+## Testing
+bUnit tests asserting rendered CSS classes for outline on/off.
+
+## Boundaries
+- Always: keep existing default rendering backwards compatible.
+- Never: change CheckboxList behavior or public API beyond the new parameter.
